---
title: Incident lifecycle (State pattern). Every other action is refused with 409 Conflict.
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> NEW : report (Employee, or Admin on behalf)
    NEW --> CLASSIFIED : classify<br/>SYSTEM on report, or Admin
    CLASSIFIED --> ASSIGNED : assign<br/>SYSTEM (strategy), or Admin
    ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : acknowledge<br/>assigned Technician
    ASSIGNED --> ASSIGNED : reassign<br/>Admin
    ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : startWork<br/>assigned Technician
    ACKNOWLEDGED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : addNote<br/>assigned Technician
    ACKNOWLEDGED --> ASSIGNED : reassign<br/>Admin
    IN_PROGRESS --> IN_PROGRESS : addNote<br/>assigned Technician
    IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : resolve<br/>assigned Technician
    IN_PROGRESS --> ASSIGNED : reassign<br/>Admin
    RESOLVED --> VERIFIED : verify<br/>reporter (Employee)
    RESOLVED --> IN_PROGRESS : reopen with reason<br/>reporter (Employee)
    VERIFIED --> CLOSED : close<br/>reporter or Admin
    CLOSED --> [*]

    note right of CLASSIFIED
        report() classifies, starts the SLA and
        asks the assignment strategy at once.
        It stays CLASSIFIED only if no skilled
        technician has free capacity.
    end note
    note right of CLOSED
        Nothing is allowed. A note on a closed
        incident gets "Cannot add a note while
        the incident is CLOSED".
    end note
